Keywords for level 1

1. / — Directory separator within file paths and as the symbol for the root directory of the unified file system.
2. CAT / Concatment — To connect or link in a series of chains.
3. LS — List the contents of a directory, displaying files and subdirectories.
4. POSIX compatibility layer / POSIX emulation layer (AKA Unix-like environment) — Compatibility layer: software that intercepts foreign API/syscalls, translates them into host OS calls, exposes a familiar interface (e.g., POSIX → Windows NT API), no hardware emulation, no guest OS, near-native performance.
5. Port — A 16-bit logical identifier (0–65535) that maps an incoming network packet to a specific process/socket on a Linux host. Pairs with an IP address to form a full socket address. Well-known ports (0–1023) are reserved for privileged services; higher ports are registered or ephemeral.
7. SSH [Secure Shell Protocol]

