So our goal is to get into a file called "Read me" in the home directory. Here is what to do, and then we will go step by step on what each thing does and how it works.

cat ./-

If you want to do it in depth, do cd which shows "current directory", then do "ls" which lists the contents of a directory, displaying files and subdirectories. Then you will see the next line just shows "-" that is the file we need.

Explanation: “cat” literally stands for “Concatenate”. It reads through the file's contents and outputs them to the standard output (the terminal).
“.” the single dot is looking through the current directory.

“/” the slash is the path separator, so when we use x command it starts it

“-” This dash is the FILE we are looking for.

So when we put them all together, we tell the console cat ./- look through our current directory and begin the search and look for "-"

This will get you your password for level 2.

